course: dictionary
lesson: 13335
title: Gusty weather
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe the weather, and their clues are in the words around them. «It was a gusty day, so Mum made us wear our coats.» The coats are a clue that the weather was cold or windy. Gusty must mean windy.
explain: «The gusty wind knocked the bins over in the street.» Knocked over is a clue that the wind was strong. Gusty means the wind blows in sudden strong bursts. Check your meaning by swapping it in: «The sudden strong bursts of wind knocked the bins over» still makes sense.
explain: Gusty is also an adjective, so it can describe a thing, like a day or a shower. Its comparison words are gusty, gustier and gustiest: «Today is gustier than yesterday.» Rarely, gusty can describe a sudden burst of laughter or a sigh, as in «She gave a gusty laugh.»
fact: Gusty weather has wind that blows in sudden strong bursts, then drops, then blows hard again.
fact: A gust is one sudden strong blow of wind.
fact: «Gusty winds» are a warning: they can knock things over, so take care on bikes, near trees and at the beach.
fact: In stories, «a gusty night» sets a wild or stormy scene.
fact: Rarely, gusty can mean a sudden loud burst, as in «a gusty laugh» or «a gusty sigh».
exercise: «It was a gusty day, so Mum made us wear our coats.» What does gusty mean here? | Quiet and still | Very wet with rain only | *Windy, with sudden strong blows of wind | Sunny and warm
exercise: «The gusty wind knocked the bins over.» What can a gusty wind do? | Make the grass grow | *Knock things over | Turn the sky blue | Melt the snow
exercise: «Gusty showers came and went all afternoon.» Find and copy the word that means the showers came in sudden bursts. | showers | came | *gusty | afternoon
test: «She gave a gusty laugh when the joke landed.» What does gusty mean here? | A long, quiet hum | *A sudden loud burst | A cold, damp feeling | A slow, soft drip
test: «Today is gustier than yesterday, so hold on to your hat.» Which word compares two days? | *gustier | hat | gusty days | gusty
exam: «The gusty winds on the beach made it hard to hold our umbrella.» Why should you take care on a gusty day? | Gusty means quiet and still | Gusty winds stop the rain | Gusty days are always warm | *Sudden strong winds can knock things over
